module probe.live_tree_disposition

data live_tree_disposition: LiveTreeDisposition = SubstrateInputsOnly

// THE WITNESS FOR THE GENERIC VERIFIED DOWNLOAD-PLUS-INSTALL EFFECT
// (gunbc.host.verified_binary_install) AND ITS SCCACHE ADAPTER
// (gunbc.host.sccache_verified_install).
//
// WHY A FILE OF ITS OWN RATHER THAN MORE CLAIMS IN THE TWO WITNESSES THAT ALREADY TOUCH sccache:
// those two prove their own narrow thing -- the elevation witness proves the non-interactive sudo
// refusal survived the migration, and test.claim.runner.runner_host_deploy_witness proves the pinned
// url and digest are named. Neither proves the two claims this migration rests on: that the effect is
// GENERIC (sccache's values arrive as PARAMETERS, so a second product can bind its own), and that a
// digest mismatch REFUSES rather than installing something anyway. A "generic" effect with one
// consumer and no second set of boundary values is a sccache-shaped string wearing a parameter list.
//
// THE BOUNDARY VALUES ARE SUPPLIED, NOT ASSUMED (DESIGN 3's witness rule). Every claim that needs a
// url, a digest, a member path or a destination reads them off the cited row (`sccache_release_0_15_0`,
// `sccache_installed_binary_path`) instead of re-typing a literal. A witness that hard-coded the
// digest it checks would keep passing after someone rotated the release and forgot the adapter --
// which is the exact failure mode this migration exists to remove.

// THE LINE THE GATE WOULD READ for a file whose bytes hash to `hex`: digest, TWO spaces, path. One
// space would parse as a different field and the gate would refuse for the wrong reason, which is the
// bug the two-space contract exists to prevent.
